>
>Similarly a lot of psychotherapy involves getting people to fill in their
>missing sumti.  For example, if someone says "I need X" (love / security /
>sex / approval etc.) possible responses are "For what?" or "What will
>happen if you don't get it?"  I would imagine this kind of thing would
>again be easier in Lojban.

A thoughtful point. This is a very clear way to explain how lojban might be
of value in psychotherapy. One might generalize it a bit by saying that
Psychotherapy involves thinking carefully about ones predications. Some
sumti are missing, some are suboptimal, some are present and optimal- but
preclude possibilities one may not have considered. Some crisp sets are
profitably reconsidered as fuzzy sets, some implicit causalities are
obscure, some hidden assumptions are unacknowledged.

